WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
hope Americans see his vision as

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:03.367
well.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.502
&gt;&gt; Now, your husband is 80 years

00:00:05.502 --> 00:00:06.170
old.
&gt;&gt; Mm-hmm.

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:08.839
&gt;&gt; If he wins a second term, he

00:00:08.839 --> 00:00:10.107
would be 82 at inauguration.

00:00:10.107 --> 00:00:11.508
What do you say to those people

00:00:11.508 --> 00:00:14.912
who say maybe he's too old to be

00:00:14.912 --> 00:00:15.379
president?

00:00:15.412 --> 00:00:16.613
Are those fair questions and

00:00:16.613 --> 00:00:17.380
conversations to be having?

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.148
&gt;&gt; I say look at what he's done.

00:00:19.148 --> 00:00:21.651
You know, look at what he's

00:00:21.651 --> 00:00:23.086
doing.

00:00:23.086 --> 00:00:26.423
Look at how physically he's got

00:00:26.423 --> 00:00:28.024
the good bill of health from the

00:00:28.024 --> 00:00:30.626
doctors to his physicals.

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:39.656
But how many 30-year-olds could

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.992
travel to Poland, get on the

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:45.095
train, go nine more hours, go to

00:00:45.495 --> 00:00:50.267
Ukraine, meet with president

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.101
zelenskyy?

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:53.503
His energy level, his level of

00:00:53.503 --> 00:00:55.505
passion, so look at the man.

00:00:55.639 --> 00:00:56.973
Look what he's doing.

00:00:57.107 --> 00:00:58.175
Look what he continues to do

00:00:58.308 --> 00:01:00.243
each and every day, and make

00:01:00.377 --> 00:01:01.511
your decision.

00:01:01.511 --> 00:01:03.513
It's up to the American people.

00:01:03.513 --> 00:01:04.781
&gt;&gt; Nikki Haley, one of the

00:01:04.915 --> 00:01:06.383
Republican candidates is calling

00:01:06.516 --> 00:01:08.852
for mental competency tests for

00:01:08.985 --> 00:01:10.353
those politicians over the age

00:01:10.487 --> 00:01:10.987
of 75.

00:01:11.087 --> 00:01:12.088
What do you think about that?

00:01:12.222 --> 00:01:13.523
&gt;&gt; It's ridiculous.

00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:14.925
&gt;&gt; Would your husband ever take

00:01:15.058 --> 00:01:16.526
one of those?

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:18.161
&gt;&gt; I mean, we haven't even

00:01:18.295 --> 00:01:19.763
discussed -- we would never even

00:01:19.896 --> 00:01:21.031
discuss something like that.

00:01:21.164 --> 00:01:22.732
&gt;&gt; You talked a little bit about

00:01:22.866 --> 00:01:24.067
your husband traveling to

00:01:24.201 --> 00:01:27.003
Ukraine and Poland this past

00:01:27.137 --> 00:01:27.537
week.

00:01:27.537 --> 00:01:29.105
You also have told us that you

00:01:29.539 --> 00:01:30.307
found out kind of last minute

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.543
that he was going to be making

00:01:33.543 --> 00:01:33.910
this secret trip --

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:36.079
&gt;&gt; Oh, absolutely.

00:01:36.213 --> 00:01:37.547
&gt;&gt; -- To Ukraine.

00:01:37.547 --> 00:01:38.014
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:01:38.014 --> 00:01:39.549
&gt;&gt; What was it like for those

00:01:39.549 --> 00:01:40.550
ten hours when he was taking

00:01:40.684 --> 00:01:41.985
that train ride into Ukraine and

00:01:42.118 --> 00:01:44.354
no one knew.

00:01:44.487 --> 00:01:47.090
How worried were you in those

00:01:47.224 --> 00:01:47.591
moments?

00:01:47.591 --> 00:01:49.626
&gt;&gt; I was of course worried, I

00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:50.259
was really worried.

00:01:50.293 --> 00:01:52.596
But you know, one thing -- and I

00:01:52.729 --> 00:01:53.830
have to say this with all my

00:01:53.964 --> 00:01:56.099
heart -- one thing that I truly

00:01:56.233 --> 00:01:57.033
believe in is the strength of

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:59.970
our military and how everything

00:02:00.103 --> 00:02:03.573
was so planned out and the

00:02:03.607 --> 00:02:06.643
secret service and what an

00:02:06.776 --> 00:02:09.846
amazing job they did in pulling

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.549
off the trip and keeping my

00:02:12.682 --> 00:02:13.583
husband safe.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:15.785
I mean, I'm watching the TV this

00:02:15.919 --> 00:02:16.987
morning and I'm seeing -- it's

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.589
just incredible what's going on

00:02:19.589 --> 00:02:21.591
in the air and in the sea, and I

00:02:21.591 --> 00:02:24.661
hope that Americans really take

00:02:24.794 --> 00:02:25.729
note of it.

00:02:25.862 --> 00:02:28.765
Like we have to give the

00:02:28.899 --> 00:02:31.768
support, all of our support to

00:02:31.902 --> 00:02:34.237
our military because of what a

00:02:34.371 --> 00:02:37.674
great job they do, and the

00:02:37.807 --> 00:02:40.110
secret service is right there

00:02:40.243 --> 00:02:40.743
hand in hand.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:42.379
&gt;&gt; Were you able to keep tabs on

00:02:42.512 --> 00:02:42.846
him --

00:02:42.846 --> 00:02:45.282
&gt;&gt; Oh, yeah.

00:02:45.615 --> 00:02:46.883
&gt;&gt; When he was -- did he

00:02:47.017 --> 00:02:47.517
communicate?

00:02:47.617 --> 00:02:47.918
&gt;&gt; Through text.

00:02:47.918 --> 00:02:51.621
&gt;&gt; Was he texting you on the

00:02:51.621 --> 00:02:53.056
train?
&gt;&gt; Well, he was -- no, he wasn't

00:02:53.189 --> 00:02:54.157
texting me on the train, but you

00:02:54.291 --> 00:02:58.128
know, it was in the back of my

00:02:58.261 --> 00:03:01.264
mind, and so I mean, I was kind

00:03:01.631 --> 00:03:04.868
of aware that he was, you know,

00:03:05.001 --> 00:03:10.440
safe and I just said a lot of

00:03:10.573 --> 00:03:10.941
prayers.

00:03:10.941 --> 00:03:13.977
&gt;&gt; Did he give you a call when

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:14.644
he made it back into Poland?

00:03:14.778 --> 00:03:15.178
&gt;&gt; Oh, yes.

00:03:15.178 --> 00:03:16.746
&gt;&gt; And what was his reflection

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:17.647
on this trip?

00:03:17.647 --> 00:03:20.884
&gt;&gt; We didn't really talk about

00:03:21.017 --> 00:03:21.885
it.
I think it will be just better

00:03:22.018 --> 00:03:22.986
to talk about it in private, you

00:03:23.119 --> 00:03:23.653
know.

00:03:23.753 --> 00:03:25.789
&gt;&gt; Yeah, have you had the chance

00:03:25.922 --> 00:03:26.523
to talk to him about this trip

00:03:26.656 --> 00:03:28.091
yet?
&gt;&gt; Oh, yeah, we've spoken a

00:03:28.224 --> 00:03:29.726
couple of times, and face timed

00:03:29.859 --> 00:03:32.195
and so, yeah, and he looks

00:03:32.329 --> 00:03:32.829
great.

00:03:32.862 --> 00:03:36.366
I mean, so he doesn't look tired

00:03:36.499 --> 00:03:36.866
or, yeah.

00:03:36.866 --> 00:03:39.970
&gt;&gt; How often do you guys face

00:03:40.103 --> 00:03:41.071
time?
&gt;&gt; I don't know, a couple times

00:03:41.204 --> 00:03:43.206
a day.

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:43.940
&gt;&gt; Even if you're just in D.C.

00:03:44.074 --> 00:03:45.108
Or when you're traveling?

00:03:45.241 --> 00:03:47.677
&gt;&gt; I'm traveling, I'm at work.

00:03:47.744 --> 00:03:50.380
I mean, he calls -- he calls a

00:03:50.513 --> 00:03:52.549
lot.
&gt;&gt; Does he call you more or do

00:03:52.682 --> 00:03:53.883
you call him more?

00:03:54.017 --> 00:03:56.586
&gt;&gt; I think he calls me more.

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:59.189
&gt;&gt; I want to turn to another

00:03:59.322 --> 00:04:01.691
issue that has come up amongst

00:04:01.691 --> 00:04:03.259
Republicans a lot, and your son

00:04:03.693 --> 00:04:04.527
hunter has really been a target

00:04:04.661 --> 00:04:06.096
for Republicans over the years

00:04:06.229 --> 00:04:08.465
and likely will be in the years

00:04:08.598 --> 00:04:09.099
to come.

00:04:09.232 --> 00:04:11.101
How does your family deal with

00:04:11.234 --> 00:04:13.069
that intense focus on hunter?

00:04:13.203 --> 00:04:16.740
&gt;&gt; We deal with it by just I

00:04:16.873 --> 00:04:20.343
guess have a different

00:04:20.477 --> 00:04:20.877
perspective.

00:04:20.877 --> 00:04:22.112
I love hunter and I'll support

00:04:22.245 --> 00:04:23.713
him in any way I can, and that's

00:04:23.713 --> 00:04:27.183
how I look at things.

00:04:27.317 --> 00:04:28.218
&gt;&gt; Has the wave of

00:04:28.351 --> 00:04:29.119
investigations into him, does

00:04:29.252 --> 00:04:30.086
that factor into any of the

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:32.589
thinking heading into 2024?

00:04:32.722 --> 00:04:34.758
&gt;&gt; No.

00:04:34.891 --> 00:04:38.695
&gt;&gt; The justice department has

00:04:38.828 --> 00:04:40.130
appointed a special counsel to

00:04:40.263 --> 00:04:41.865
look into the way your husband

00:04:41.998 --> 00:04:42.565
handled classified documents

00:04:42.699 --> 00:04:43.733
when he left the vice

00:04:43.733 --> 00:04:44.067
presidencies.

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:44.834
When did you first find out

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:45.835
about these documents?

00:04:45.969 --> 00:04:51.041
Were you surprised?

00:04:51.174 --> 00:04:51.741
&gt;&gt; Probably when the rest of

00:04:51.875 --> 00:04:52.275
America did.

00:04:52.275 --> 00:04:52.775
I was really surprised.

00:04:52.876 --> 00:04:56.379
We had no idea, and so I think

00:04:56.513 --> 00:04:58.715
we found out when everyone else

00:04:58.848 --> 00:04:59.149
did.

00:04:59.149 --> 00:05:00.917
&gt;&gt; Where in the house were they?

00:05:01.051 --> 00:05:02.886
Were they in a secure location?

00:05:03.019 --> 00:05:04.120
Did people have access to them?

00:05:04.254 --> 00:05:10.160
&gt;&gt; Well, I think they were at

00:05:10.293 --> 00:05:11.761
the Biden Penn center.

00:05:11.761 --> 00:05:12.362
&gt;&gt; And there were some at your

00:05:12.495 --> 00:05:15.065
home in Wilmington.

00:05:15.198 --> 00:05:16.499
&gt;&gt; And I think those were in the

00:05:16.633 --> 00:05:18.001
garage, believe me, Arlette, I

00:05:18.134 --> 00:05:18.935
don't have time to go through

00:05:19.069 --> 00:05:20.570
the boxes in the garage.

00:05:20.703 --> 00:05:22.105
We had no idea they were even

00:05:22.238 --> 00:05:22.738
down there.

00:05:22.839 --> 00:05:25.141
&gt;&gt; I wanted to turn back to one

00:05:25.275 --> 00:05:28.111
campaign question.

00:05:28.244 --> 00:05:30.046
You and I --

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:30.780
&gt;&gt; You're not giving up.

00:05:30.914 --> 00:05:32.248
&gt;&gt; No, I'm not giving up.

00:05:32.382 --> 00:05:33.783
&gt;&gt; You're saying everyone's

00:05:33.883 --> 00:05:34.551
asking you.

00:05:34.684 --> 00:05:35.184
There you go.

00:05:35.285 --> 00:05:36.753
&gt;&gt; Everyone's asking you.

00:05:36.886 --> 00:05:38.354
Do you ever worry about how

00:05:38.488 --> 00:05:40.957
grueling a campaign might be on

00:05:41.091 --> 00:05:43.159
him?
&gt;&gt; I think everyone campaign is

00:05:43.293 --> 00:05:43.793
grueling.

00:05:43.793 --> 00:05:45.829
I don't care whether you're 20,

00:05:45.962 --> 00:05:46.729
30 or whatever age.

00:05:46.863 --> 00:05:49.399
Campaigns now have become really

00:05:49.799 --> 00:05:50.967
grueling.
And Arlette, you know, you've

00:05:51.101 --> 00:05:53.837
been on a lot of campaigns.

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:55.972
You have to see the difference

00:05:56.106 --> 00:06:01.444
between even ten years ago and

00:06:01.811 --> 00:06:02.479
today.
&gt;&gt; I know you guys are really

00:06:02.612 --> 00:06:03.379
big into these family meetings.

00:06:03.813 --> 00:06:05.949
&gt;&gt; Uh-huh.

00:06:06.082 --> 00:06:06.816
&gt;&gt; Was there one definitive

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:08.985
family meeting that, okay woorgs

00:06:09.119 --> 00:06:11.054
ere doing this or has this been

00:06:11.187 --> 00:06:11.821
a rolling conversation?

00:06:11.821 --> 00:06:12.922
&gt;&gt; It's been rolling this time.

00:06:13.056 --> 00:06:14.991
Last time we did have a family

00:06:15.125 --> 00:06:16.092
meeting, and we've had family

00:06:16.226 --> 00:06:17.327
meetings other times, but it's

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:18.294
sort of rolling just because of

00:06:18.428 --> 00:06:21.331
the pace of our lives, and so if

00:06:21.831 --> 00:06:23.233
I can grab two grandkids here

00:06:23.366 --> 00:06:24.534
and say, hey, what are you

00:06:24.667 --> 00:06:27.237
thinking about, what are your

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:28.638
thoughts or, you know, our

00:06:28.771 --> 00:06:29.139
daughter.

00:06:29.139 --> 00:06:30.406
So I'm sort of keeping tabs.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.242
&gt;&gt; So in your mind, this is

00:06:32.375 --> 00:06:32.742
happening?

00:06:32.742 --> 00:06:35.512
&gt;&gt; Absolutely.

00:06:35.845 --> 00:06:36.345
You want to come?

00:06:36.379 --> 00:06:37.847
You want to come on the trail?

00:06:37.847 --> 00:06:41.017
&gt;&gt; I might be covering you guys

00:06:41.151 --> 00:06:41.851
on the trail again.

00:06:41.851 --> 00:06:43.119
&gt;&gt; Oh, good, good.

00:06:43.253 --> 00:06:46.322
&gt;&gt; We are back now with Arlette.

00:06:46.456 --> 00:06:50.560
We're also joined luckily by

00:06:50.693 --> 00:06:52.462
Audi Cornish and Abby Phillip.

00:06:52.595 --> 00:06:53.897
Arlette, I'm going to start with

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:55.865
you.
So you asked all of the

00:06:55.865 --> 00:06:56.733
questions that I think the

00:06:56.866 --> 00:06:58.434
American public has been

00:06:58.568 --> 00:07:00.270
discussing about Joe Biden, and

00:07:00.403 --> 00:07:03.873
then you get into what Jill

00:07:03.873 --> 00:07:04.307
Biden has been up to.

00:07:04.307 --> 00:07:06.309
Were you surprised by any of her

00:07:06.442 --> 00:07:06.776
answers?

00:07:06.776 --> 00:07:07.877
&gt;&gt; You know, I think that her

00:07:07.944 --> 00:07:09.979
answer regarding 2024 is quite

00:07:10.113 --> 00:07:10.513
interesting.

00:07:10.513 --> 00:07:11.881
I think the way that she

00:07:11.881 --> 00:07:12.382
answered that question really

00:07:12.515 --> 00:07:14.784
makes it seem as if it's not a

00:07:14.918 --> 00:07:16.986
matter of if but when this

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:18.354
campaign will be launched, but

00:07:18.488 --> 00:07:20.256
she also does leave an opening

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:22.292
for him should he decide not to

00:07:22.425 --> 00:07:23.893
run in 2024.

00:07:23.893 --> 00:07:26.963
You know, she says it's Joe's

00:07:27.096 --> 00:07:27.463
decision.

00:07:27.463 --> 00:07:30.266
That they'll support him if he

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:31.901
does, but then she says if he

00:07:32.001 --> 00:07:33.069
decides to do something else,

00:07:33.203 --> 00:07:34.170
we'll also support him there.

00:07:34.304 --> 00:07:35.371
It kind of provides you a little

00:07:35.505 --> 00:07:36.573
bit of answer both ways.

00:07:36.706 --> 00:07:37.974
These conversations that I had

00:07:38.107 --> 00:07:40.009
with her over the course of

00:07:40.143 --> 00:07:40.910
those five days in Africa, it

00:07:41.044 --> 00:07:42.278
really does seem like things are

00:07:42.412 --> 00:07:44.914
moving towards him running for

00:07:45.048 --> 00:07:45.915
re-election again in the coming

00:07:45.915 --> 00:07:47.016
months.
&gt;&gt; I do want to ask about this

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:47.917
controversy -- I don't know if

00:07:48.051 --> 00:07:49.452
that's what to call it -- but

00:07:49.586 --> 00:07:50.853
over age, it's come up and again

00:07:50.987 --> 00:07:53.089
and again, and Nikki Haley purkd

00:07:53.223 --> 00:07:54.991
it to a whole 'nother level when

00:07:55.124 --> 00:07:56.793
she talked about a competency

00:07:56.926 --> 00:07:57.227
test.

00:07:57.227 --> 00:08:05.935
Joe Biden -- Jill Biden

00:08:05.935 --> 00:08:08.638
responded with it's ridiculous.

00:08:08.771 --> 00:08:09.372
&gt;&gt; She's been in this game for a

00:08:09.505 --> 00:08:10.306
very long time.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.241
It's a little bit different from

00:08:11.374 --> 00:08:15.011
first lady Michelle Obama who

00:08:15.144 --> 00:08:16.312
married someone who was not in

00:08:16.446 --> 00:08:19.182
public life when they first got

00:08:19.315 --> 00:08:19.815
together.

00:08:19.949 --> 00:08:20.950
Jill Biden's been in this for a

00:08:21.084 --> 00:08:22.552
while.
It also underscores the problem

00:08:22.685 --> 00:08:24.120
for them.

00:08:24.254 --> 00:08:25.555
Here they are, she's on a trip

00:08:25.955 --> 00:08:27.123
visiting countries in Africa.

00:08:27.257 --> 00:08:28.758
The posture that this

00:08:28.891 --> 00:08:29.959
administration has had towards

00:08:29.959 --> 00:08:31.361
Africa is radically different

00:08:31.494 --> 00:08:32.061
than the prior administration.

00:08:32.195 --> 00:08:33.563
But it's a conversation that

00:08:33.963 --> 00:08:38.635
can't be had because not only

00:08:38.768 --> 00:08:40.203
are people focused on whether

00:08:40.336 --> 00:08:40.870
he's going to run but even

00:08:41.004 --> 00:08:41.604
asking the question should he at

00:08:41.971 --> 00:08:42.338
all because of his age.

00:08:42.338 --> 00:08:43.072
I mean, that really gives you a

00:08:43.206 --> 00:08:44.240
sense of the kind of obstacles

00:08:44.374 --> 00:08:44.874
for them.

00:08:44.874 --> 00:08:45.975
&gt;&gt; It also struck me that she

00:08:45.975 --> 00:08:48.444
was answering the question over

00:08:48.578 --> 00:08:49.979
and over again at every chance

00:08:50.013 --> 00:08:53.116
she got, even when Arlette

00:08:53.249 --> 00:08:54.050
wasn't asking her about it.

00:08:54.183 --> 00:08:55.518
&gt;&gt; She was ready with an answer.

00:08:55.652 --> 00:08:57.053
&gt;&gt; She's talking about the

00:08:57.186 --> 00:08:57.987
Ukraine trip, she's talking

00:08:57.987 --> 00:08:59.155
about his stamina, his ability

00:08:59.289 --> 00:08:59.989
to do all of that.

00:09:00.123 --> 00:09:01.991
I mean, I think she is keenly

00:09:02.125 --> 00:09:04.360
aware that this is an

00:09:04.494 --> 00:09:05.361
unavoidable question about her

00:09:05.495 --> 00:09:08.164
husband, and she is injecting at

00:09:08.298 --> 00:09:09.198
every moment an opportunity to

00:09:09.332 --> 00:09:11.567
say, this is a guy who can keep

00:09:12.001 --> 00:09:15.004
This is a guy who has what it
up.

